# The three docs generated from the tree and committed.
#
# `union` keeps both sides' lines instead of conflicting. For a file that is one
# line per fact that is usually the right answer outright, and where it isn't
# (both sides rewrote the same `+N more` counter) the result is a duplicate line
# that the post-merge hook regenerates away and CI's --check catches. Never
# blocking, never silently wrong for long.
#
# It replaced a custom `generated-doc` driver that regenerated properly but had
# to be registered per clone (npm postinstall), which GitHub's servers do not
# run: every open PR showed a conflict in these files on every merge to main,
# while the same merge was clean on any developer's machine. `union` is built
# into git and needs no config, so GitHub honors it too.
#
# CLAUDE.md is deliberately NOT here. It is prose, where union would duplicate
# paragraphs rather than facts; the generated numbers that used to live in it
# are docs/repo-stats.md for exactly that reason.
docs/module-map.md merge=union
docs/screen-map.md merge=union
docs/repo-stats.md merge=union
